<p>Each till has its own receipt settings in <strong>Settings → Tills</strong>.</p>

<h2>Printing from the browser (the default)</h2>
<p>Any printer your computer can print to will work. Receipts open in the browser's print window, sized for 80 mm thermal paper. Choose the printer once and tick "don't ask again" if your browser offers it. To open the cash drawer on each receipt, turn on "open cash drawer" in the printer's driver settings.</p>

<h2>Printing silently through QZ Tray</h2>
<p><a href="https://qz.io" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">QZ Tray</a> is a small free program that lets HardPoint send receipts straight to a thermal printer, without the print window, and open the cash drawer on cash sales. Install it on the till computer, then set the till's print mode to <strong>QZ Tray</strong> and type the printer's name exactly as the computer shows it. Choose the paper width: 58 mm printers fit 32 characters a line, 80 mm printers 42 or 48.</p>

<h2>Customer display</h2>
<p>Open <strong>Customer display</strong> from the till's menu in a second window and drag it to a screen facing the customer. It shows each item and the total as you ring them up.</p>

<h2>Barcode scanners</h2>
<p>USB and Bluetooth scanners that type like a keyboard work without any setup. Scan on the till screen and the product is added to the sale.</p>
